<title>UK: ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</title>
<headline>ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) said the 4,250 tonne buffer-stock sale earlier on Thursday was completed at the following prices.</p>
<p> ORIGIN	TONNES QUALITY  CROP YEAR   PORT    US DLR</p>
<p>PRICE/TONNE</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire 1,636    GF	1981/82  Rotterdam   $1,551</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   350    FF	1981/82  Rotterdam   $1,493</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   199    GF	1987/88  Rotterdam   $1,569</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   100    FF	1987/88  Rotterdam   $1,510</p>
<p>Nigeria	   647    GF	1986/87  Rotterdam   $1,556-1,580</p>
<p>Nigeria	   255    FF	1986/87  Rotterdam   $1,510</p>
<p>Nigeria	    50    FF	1987/88  Rotterdam   $1,510</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   100   FAQ	1980/81  Amsterdam   $1,390</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   312   FAQ	1981/82  Amsterdam   $1,390</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   601   FAQ	1987/88  Amsterdam   $1,413-1,460</p>
<p>(GF=good fermented, FF=fair fermented, FAQ=fair average quality)</p>
<p>The ICCO said these prices are for prompt delivery.</p>
<p>--Medora Lee, London newsroom +44 171 542 8072</p>
